# Git Commit Rules

Message format is enforced by commitlint (`@commitlint/config-conventional` via `.husky/commit-msg`).
Do not maintain a parallel type/format list in this file.

## Agent / process (not enforced by commitlint)

- Messages in English; imperative subject; one logical change per commit
- Prefer a short subject-only message. Add a body only for large refactors, multi-subsystem changes, or breaking changes — skip detailed descriptions for routine work
- Do not push without explicit user approval
- Never commit secrets, debug junk, unrelated files, or local artifacts
- Before commit: review the staged diff; hooks cover staged lint/format and (on push) typecheck/lint/format/test — still run a targeted check when the change is narrow and you need faster feedback

## Hooks (reference)

| Hook | Command |
| ---- | ------- |
| `pre-commit` | `lint-staged` (ESLint + Prettier on staged files) |
| `commit-msg` | `commitlint` |
| `pre-push` | `pnpm typecheck && pnpm lint && pnpm format:check && pnpm test` |
